From: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:04:02 +0100
Subject: [M150] [maglev] Don't reuse outer kReceiver call feedback in reduced
 apply

Original change's description:
> [maglev] Don't reuse outer kReceiver call feedback in reduced apply
>
> For a direct `fn.apply(this, args)` call, BuildCallWithFeedback
> already checks that the `kReceiver` feedback target is a JSFunction
> and passes it to TryReduceFunctionPrototypeApplyCallWithReceiver.
> However, TryReduceFunctionPrototypeApply also read the current
> speculation feedback and treated any `kReceiver` target as the
> receiver of `apply`. When `Function.prototype.apply` is reached via
> an outer `Function.prototype.call` or `Function.prototype.apply`
> reduction (such as `Function.prototype.apply.call(x)`), that
> feedback belongs to the outer call rather than the inner `apply`,
> and can even hold a FeedbackCell like `many_closures_cell`.
>
> Pass an empty receiver target from TryReduceFunctionPrototypeApply,
> and tighten TryReduceFunctionPrototypeApplyCallWithReceiver to take
> an OptionalJSFunctionRef.
>
